1
00:00:00,792 --> 00:00:04,796
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,679
[Nimfa] <i>I may have done the wrong thing.</i>

3
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:16,391
<i>-But there's no turning back now.</i>
-[Camia grunts]

4
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:18,101
<i>-Hello, Ma'am Emilia!</i>
<i>-Nimfa!</i>

5
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:21,980
[Ivy] <i>The truth is that we came</i>
<i>to ask for your endorsement</i>

6
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:24,190
<i>so that Arnaldo could join your party.</i>

7
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:26,025
[Arnaldo] <i>I don't care</i>
<i>about the endorsement!</i>

8
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:28,361
<i>I'll form my own party for all I care,</i>

9
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,447
<i>just stop acting like a cheap whore--</i>

10
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,241
<i>How dare you say that to me?</i>

11
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:35,160
[Emilia] <i>Does your fiancée</i>
<i>really love you?</i>

12
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:36,661
<i>Maybe she brought you here…</i>

13
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>-to set you up.</i>
<i>-Shut up!</i>

14
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:42,041
<i>Okay, go ahead. Follow her!</i>

15
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:46,421
<i>That way, you'll see that</i>
<i>she doesn't really love you.</i>

16
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:49,215
<i>Ivy, it's Nimfa. She's the one who</i>
<i>told Emilia that Lily is still alive.</i>

17
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,676
[Arnaldo] <i>How long have you been</i>
<i>meeting with Diego?</i>

18
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:52,927
[Camia] <i>Nimfa got away.</i>

19
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:57,390
<i>I'm sure she'll go to Emilia</i>
<i>and tell her who Ivy really is.</i>

20
00:00:57,474 --> 00:01:00,810
[Ivy] <i>Diego is just a friend.</i>
<i>If you don't believe me,</i>

21
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,646
<i>if you think I'm betraying you,</i>
<i>let's just stop this.</i>

22
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,690
<i>We should call off our wedding.</i>

23
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>You just broke my heart.</i>

24
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>We should spend some time apart.</i>

25
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:11,404
<i>So, you're Mom's spy.</i>

26
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,948
<i>I need to tell her</i>
<i>something about Miss Ivy.</i>

27
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:16,951
<i>You shouldn't trust her.</i>
<i>She's just using you.</i>

28
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,495
<i>You need to know that Ivy is--</i>

29
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:21,706
<i>-That's not true!</i>
-[gunshots]

30
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:23,541
[Diego] <i>Nimfa is Emilia's spy.</i>

31
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:26,252
<i>She was bribed with money</i>
<i>and other things.</i>

32
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:30,131
<i>Emilia told her to spy on our party</i>
<i>and sabotage my campaign.</i>

33
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:31,758
<i>My daughter wouldn't do that!</i>

34
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:33,510
[Ivy] <i>You killed Nimfa?</i>

35
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:35,637
[Arnaldo] <i>I killed for you.</i>
<i>That's how much I love you.</i>

36
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,972
<i>We will only get married</i>

37
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,974
<i>if you believe me</i>

38
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:42,185
<i>when I say I'm not</i>
<i>a traitor to your family.</i>

39
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:45,563
<i>I'm worried because my spy</i>

40
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:47,774
<i>hasn't checked in with me yet.</i>

41
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:50,235
<i>Nimfa is dead, and I killed her.</i>

42
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:56,908
Why did you do that?!

43
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,327
Why did you do that?!

44
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:02,205
Don't you know that
I was using her to find out--

45
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,873
To find out what?!

46
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:06,918
What exactly do you want to know?!

47
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:10,171
Tell me! To chase some
evidence that doesn't exist

48
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,172
to ruin Ivy's reputation?!

49
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:12,674
Well, guess what?!

50
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:15,385
Your spy didn't discover a thing! Nothing!

51
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:16,761
I don't believe you!

52
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,972
Nimfa tried to call me several times!

53
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:21,182
If she didn't know anything,
then why would she call me?!

54
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:22,267
That's impossible!

55
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:25,061
I know she discovered something
about your beloved Ivy!

56
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:27,856
Well, I've nothing to say to you.

57
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,525
Well, except that she begged
for her life. That's it.

58
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:33,027
-Enough!
-Damn right, I've had enough!

59
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:36,364
I'm sick of all of you meddling
in my affairs, especially you!

60
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:39,826
Hey! You benefited from my interference!

61
00:02:39,909 --> 00:02:41,744
Because of that,

62
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:44,205
I was able to intercept
Diego's campaign plans!

63
00:02:44,289 --> 00:02:45,748
Get that through
that thick skull of yours!

64
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:48,751
Everything you do also
benefits you! Right?!

65
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,547
You wanted to know if
Ivy's funding their campaign.

66
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:54,132
Am I right?!

67
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,593
In spite of me telling you
to back off, you kept pushing!

68
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:59,637
You even went out of your way
to have her raped?!

69
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:01,723
Now, Nimfa is dead.

70
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:05,518
And, that is the price
you had to pay for what you did.

71
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:07,186
We're even.

72
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:11,232
[tense music playing]

73
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,574
Well, that cleared the air.

74
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:29,375
[Diego] <i>That bastard!</i>

75
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,586
He's rotten to the core!

76
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,924
Ivy, I'm going after Arnaldo.

77
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:37,926
I'll make him pay!

78
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,055
Please forgive me, Diego.

79
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,683
Because of me, Nimfa's gone.

80
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:47,894
That's not true.

81
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:51,022
Diego, Nimfa discovered my secret.

82
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:52,941
That secret put her life in danger.

83
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:54,484
That's why she was killed!

84
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:57,487
No. This wouldn't have happened to Nimfa

85
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,447
if it weren't for the Ardientes!

86
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:02,742
<i>You did nothing wrong, Ivy.</i>
<i>Don't blame yourself.</i>

87
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:04,786
We'll file a case against them.

88
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:08,081
But no one witnessed
Nimfa's murder, Diego.

89
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:12,752
Arnaldo already disposed of her body too.

90
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:17,548
[Ivy] <i>Diego, if there's no</i>
<i>evidence, then there's no case.</i>

91
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:21,427
[faucet running]

92
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:24,889
-[gunshots]
-[Arnaldo screaming]

93
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:49,163
[no audible dialogue]

94
00:04:56,421 --> 00:05:00,633
[desolate music playing]

95
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:24,741
<i>Dad…</i>

96
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,868
<i>the witnesses…</i>

97
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:30,038
<i>Nanny Carlotta…</i>

98
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,207
<i>And now, Nimfa…</i>

99
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:38,629
<i>They're just some of</i>
<i>the Ardientes' victims.</i>

100
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:43,134
<i>Tonight, I'm lighting a candle…</i>

101
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:45,470
<i>for Nimfa…</i>

102
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,139
<i>for all of them.</i>

103
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:52,852
<i>To pay my respects and extend my sympathy…</i>

104
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:57,148
<i>and to promise that it will not end here.</i>

105
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:05,198
[Loring] Hey, there's food
at the back, okay?

106
00:06:05,281 --> 00:06:08,034
Don't be shy. Help yourselves
to some coffee and food.

107
00:06:08,117 --> 00:06:08,910
[man] Okay, ma'am.

108
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:10,870
-Here you go.
-Oh, thank you.

109
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:12,997
Oh, I'm really worried.

110
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:14,874
[sighs]

111
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:17,293
I really hope they find Nimfa,

112
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,838
so Diego won't feel sad anymore.

113
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,800
I hope so too. I wonder where Nimfa is.

114
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:25,134
According to Diego,

115
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:28,679
she ran away…

116
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:31,474
and headed to the
mansion of the Ardientes.

117
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:34,268
Hey, come here and have
something to eat, Diego.

118
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:35,603
[Loring] Come.

119
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:41,317
What's wrong, Diego?

120
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:43,778
Is there a problem?

121
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:46,989
Diego?

122
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:49,992
Nanny, Uncle…

123
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:54,122
There's something you need to know.

124
00:06:56,874 --> 00:07:01,546
[man whistling]

125
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:08,761
This area's so filthy. Hey! Shoo!

126
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:12,723
There's a lot of trash here.

127
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:14,725
It's like this every day.

128
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,019
What's this? This thing is huge.

129
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:18,062
I wonder what's inside.

130
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:23,484
[gasps]

131
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:24,610
It's a hand!

132
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,946
Help! There's a corpse here!

133
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:30,616
Help! Everyone! Come here!

134
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,036
Everyone, help!

135
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,122
[man] There's a corpse here!

136
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:37,665
-What's wrong?!
-There's a body here!

137
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:39,208
-What?
-Oh, no.

138
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:41,210
-Miss Loring!
-I don't know!

139
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,211
-Miss Loring!
-I saw a hand…

140
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:43,254
[man] …when I picked it up!

141
00:07:43,337 --> 00:07:44,130
Miss Loring!

142
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:45,798
-Is this about Nimfa?
-Miss Loring!

143
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:46,757
[woman] Miss Loring!

144
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:50,386
There's a commotion outside.
They found a body!

145
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,804
-What?!
-A body!

146
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:52,889
[Pandoy] What?!

147
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:55,349
[woman 2] Call the police!

148
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,560
There's a body here! Police!

149
00:07:57,643 --> 00:07:58,686
[Loring] What?!

150
00:07:58,769 --> 00:07:59,729
[man] I don't know!

151
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:01,647
I was just getting the trash.

152
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:06,819
[Pandoy] Who-- Does anyone
know who dumped this here?

153
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:08,696
I don't know! I was just getting the trash

154
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:10,072
when I saw a hand!

155
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:13,534
And when I looked closer, I saw a corpse!

156
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:15,036
Who is this, Diego?!

157
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:17,872
Diego?!

158
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:31,385
[desolate music playing]

159
00:08:55,576 --> 00:08:57,787
[Loring weeping]

160
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:00,248
[man] Oh, no.

161
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:02,291
[Loring] Nimfa!

162
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,794
[Loring crying]

163
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:11,425
[Loring crying]

164
00:09:15,054 --> 00:09:16,347
It's Fernan! Fernan!

165
00:09:16,764 --> 00:09:18,057
[Loring] What happened?

166
00:09:18,432 --> 00:09:19,850
-Fernan!
-Fernan!

167
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:23,813
-Nimfa!
-Fernan!

168
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:26,148
-Nimfa! Nimfa!
-[Loring screams]

169
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:26,983
-Mister Fernan.
-Nimfa!

170
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:29,360
[Diego] Mister Fernan. Mister Fernan.

171
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:30,528
[Fernan weeping]

172
00:09:30,611 --> 00:09:32,488
-Nimfa!
-Calm down, sir.

173
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:33,948
-[Fernan weeping]
-Please calm down.

174
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,283
She's my daughter!

175
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:37,368
Nimfa!

176
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:41,122
Nimfa!

177
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:44,250
[Fernan weeping]

178
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:50,798
Nimfa! My dear!

179
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:55,052
Let me go, Diego!

180
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,971
Diego, please!

181
00:09:57,054 --> 00:10:01,601
[Fernan weeping]

182
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:09,191
What did they do to my daughter?!

183
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:21,370
Nimfa!

184
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,666
Nimfa!

185
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:28,878
[Loring] Miss Camia…

186
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,886
Who did this to you?!

187
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:38,638
Tell me!

188
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:48,147
Nimfa!

189
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:57,573
[indistinct chatter]

190
00:10:58,157 --> 00:10:59,992
[Loring weeping]

191
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:05,665
-Take that away.
-The ambulance is here.

192
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:06,791
[Fernan] Nimfa!

193
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:09,585
-Nimfa!
-Come on. Carry her.

194
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:12,838
[Loring and Fernan weeping]

195
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:14,799
[Fernan] Nimfa!

196
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:20,930
Nimfa!

197
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:39,740
[tense music playing]

198
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:45,121
Nimfa, dear! Nimfa! Nimfa!

199
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:47,331
-Nimfa!
-Let's go.

200
00:11:47,415 --> 00:11:48,332
Nimfa!

201
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,085
Nimfa!

202
00:11:57,258 --> 00:12:01,762
[ambulance siren blaring]

203
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:06,767
Nimfa!

204
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:27,913
<i>This is just the beginning, Diego.</i>

205
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:38,257
[police officer] Do you know the victim?

206
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:41,510
Nimfa was my childhood friend.

207
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:44,096
-When did you last see her?
-We were together last night.

208
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:45,931
But she ran away.

209
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,767
I know who did this.

210
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:52,396
Arnaldo Ardiente killed her!

211
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:54,732
He killed my friend!

212
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:58,402
Okay, then. I'll need
your official statement,

213
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,779
and if your statement
matches the results of

214
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:03,365
the fingerprint test on the gun,
we'll know who the killer is.

215
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:07,745
Diego.

216
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:18,214
My daughter is gone!

217
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:20,716
[Loring] Get him some water. Fernan.

218
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:22,718
-Pandoy.
-Sit down. Sit down. Please.

219
00:13:22,801 --> 00:13:24,803
-Mister Fernan.
-Sit. Sit down.

220
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,181
Here's the water.

221
00:13:29,266 --> 00:13:31,310
-Fernan.
-Give me back my daughter!

222
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:33,896
[Fernan weeping]

223
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:37,733
My daughter!

224
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:41,070
Mister Fernan, drink this.

225
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:42,905
Fernan, drink some water.

226
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:49,328
I heard the Ardientes killed my daughter!

227
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,581
Is it because she's connected to Emilia?

228
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:55,125
Someone tell me the truth!

229
00:13:56,835 --> 00:13:58,754
Mister Fernan, we don't have proof.

230
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,381
But you're right.

231
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,551
The Ardientes are responsible for this.

232
00:14:05,678 --> 00:14:06,637
Don't worry.

233
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,764
-My poor daughter.
-We'll make them pay.

234
00:14:09,765 --> 00:14:11,058
Their day will come.

235
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:13,769
[Camia] Diego…

236
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:17,606
of all the places here
in Poblacion Ardiente,

237
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:21,360
why did they put Nimfa's body
in front of your headquarters?

238
00:14:21,443 --> 00:14:23,863
[ominous music playing]

239
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,489
I feel this was all planned.

240
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:27,408
I can only think of two things.

241
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:32,079
It's either they'll have
me killed or have me framed up.

242
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:34,748
[Diego] This can't happen.

243
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,042
I need to act fast.

244
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:40,963
Mister Fernan, don't worry.

245
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:45,134
I'll do everything to
bring justice to Nimfa's death.

246
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,137
My daughter…

247
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:50,890
[Fernan] Why…

248
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:05,863
Hon…

249
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:11,201
I was just thinking…

250
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:13,370
so many things have happened.

251
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:15,998
I'm so stressed out.

252
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,459
Then, I realized

253
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,879
that maybe we can speed up the wedding.

254
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:26,467
Speed it up?

255
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:29,511
I like it.

256
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:35,059
But, I'm actually curious
as to why you'd want that.

257
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:38,187
[upbeat music playing]

258
00:15:39,229 --> 00:15:41,273
Because Nimfa's death…

259
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,319
made me realize life really is short.

260
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:50,991
That's why I want to get
married as soon as possible.

261
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:54,787
As soon as possible, hon.

262
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:57,998
I love you.

263
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:04,380
Oh, really?

264
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:07,883
You mean, you don't hate me

265
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,010
despite knowing that I was
the one who killed Nimfa?

266
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:13,430
No, hon.

267
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:15,766
Never.

268
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,310
Because you're the only
one who could do that.

269
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:21,105
And you only did that for me.

270
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:24,191
So, Arnaldo…

271
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:26,068
[sinister music playing]

272
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,903
I want us to get married right away.

273
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:31,115
I love you.

274
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:37,788
[sighs] What's with that look?

275
00:16:37,871 --> 00:16:39,957
It's like you don't believe me.

276
00:16:40,624 --> 00:16:41,834
No, I actually believe you.

277
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,670
-Really?
-I do.

278
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:49,883
Thank you.

279
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:54,138
[sinister music continues]

280
00:16:54,221 --> 00:16:55,305
I love you.

281
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:00,894
I said I love you.

282
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:03,564
I love you too.

283
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:06,025
Hmm.

284
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,278
I love you too.

285
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:23,125
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

286
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,627
[Claire] Diego! What are you doing here?!

287
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:26,754
Where's Arnaldo?

288
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:30,632
Do you remember the
last time you were here?

289
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,385
You never learn, do you?

290
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:36,847
Arnaldo! You monster!
What did you do to Nimfa?!

291
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:37,681
Nimfa?

292
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:39,224
I don't know what you're talking about.

293
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,392
You liar!

294
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:42,770
You think you can get away with this

295
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:44,104
just because you're the mayor?

296
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:49,026
I won't stop until I
make you pay for this!

297
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:50,778
-You bastard!
-[laughs viciously]

298
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:53,906
[Arnaldo chuckles]

299
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:57,201
-Diego…
-Hon…

300
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,911
No, I'm okay.

301
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:03,957
I was just about to say that…

302
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:07,044
if you want justice for Nimfa's death,

303
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,880
don't worry. You'll get it.

304
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,008
Soon.

305
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,180
[Arnaldo laughs viciously]

306
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:19,473
[Arnaldo] Whoa!

307
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:20,849
Take it easy. This coat's new.

308
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,559
[Arnaldo sighs]

309
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:38,033
<i>I don't know what game</i>
<i>you're playing, Arnaldo.</i>

310
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:42,162
<i>But I promise you, I will take you down.</i>

311
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:46,834
<i>I'll have the last laugh.</i>

312
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:59,930
[Ivy] Hon? Surprise!

313
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:03,058
-Hi, Honey!
-Hi!

314
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,311
-Mm…
-[Arnaldo] Uh…

315
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,188
What's this? Who are they?

316
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:09,857
Oh, um…

317
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:12,276
This is Charlie and Monet.

318
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:13,527
They're designers.

319
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:16,780
I want you to choose
your suit for our wedding.

320
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:20,242
Okay, but isn't it too early for that?

321
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:22,661
Excuse me.

322
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:25,372
Come on, hon. Too early?

323
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:30,961
We haven't even set
the date of our wedding.

324
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:35,090
Well then, let's set a date.

325
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,050
[moans]

326
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,218
But before that…

327
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,222
I want to get married as soon as possible

328
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:44,725
because I'm scared of Diego's threat.

329
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:49,396
But I know you can handle Diego, hon.

330
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:55,485
Especially when you said that
Nimfa's about to get justice.

331
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:57,196
The question is…

332
00:19:58,405 --> 00:19:59,406
How?

333
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:04,494
Hon, sit down.

334
00:20:06,955 --> 00:20:09,041
Don't worry about that, okay?

335
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:10,918
[nervous laugh]

336
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:14,338
Let me see your designs. Okay.

337
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:16,757
Help me choose, then.

338
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:20,886
Charlie, Monet, sit down.

339
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:29,019
[Arnaldo] Do you like this? It's green.

340
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:49,414
There are rumors going around that

341
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:50,832
the Ardiente family has an armory,

342
00:20:51,541 --> 00:20:54,044
full of unlicensed and unregistered guns.

343
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:55,837
Good thing you reported this
to the Manila office.

344
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,631
Otherwise, this would've been ignored.

345
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:00,759
Detective, conspiracy
has become the norm here.

346
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,970
That's why we asked for your help.

347
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:04,346
And one more thing.

348
00:21:04,429 --> 00:21:07,349
If the gun used to kill your friend

349
00:21:07,432 --> 00:21:08,976
matches a gun in that armory,

350
00:21:09,059 --> 00:21:11,645
that would be strong evidence
to incriminate the Ardientes,

351
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:13,814
not only in the killing of Nimfa.

352
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:16,608
We can trace various crimes
committed in this town

353
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:17,859
using those firearms.

354
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:19,778
Thank you, Attorney.

355
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:21,947
[detective] <i>This is solid</i>
<i>evidence, Mr. Torillo.</i>

356
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:24,324
<i>This is our priority operation.</i>

357
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:27,327
<i>We'll raid this armory</i>
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

358
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,345
[goon] Congressman, someone's coming!

359
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:48,015
They're armed! Special forces from Manila.

360
00:21:48,473 --> 00:21:49,516
[rapid gunfire]

361
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:51,852
[rapid gunfire]

362
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:56,148
[suspenseful music playing]

363
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,108
<i>The Ardientes are finally</i>

364
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:01,028
<i>going to pay for their crimes.</i>

365
00:22:02,904 --> 00:22:04,239
Open fire.

366
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,283
Buy us some time. Go!

367
00:22:06,366 --> 00:22:07,451
Yes, sir.

368
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:08,577
Hurry up.

369
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:12,622
[suspenseful music continues]

370
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,334
-[gunshots]
-[man grunts]

371
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:18,920
[Julio] Faster.

372
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:32,017
[rapid gunfire]

373
00:22:43,612 --> 00:22:44,696
Move! Move!

374
00:22:46,073 --> 00:22:47,074
Search the area.

375
00:22:58,293 --> 00:22:59,336
Sir, negative.

376
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:03,423
Okay. Move.

377
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:17,646
ARDIENTES' HIDDEN ARMORY RAIDED

378
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,774
Diego, look.

379
00:23:21,316 --> 00:23:23,235
I know this will add to your good record

380
00:23:23,318 --> 00:23:27,072
because you had their
hidden armory raided.

381
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:30,450
Atty. Fisher, we can
use this against them.

382
00:23:30,992 --> 00:23:33,745
Let's add this to our evidence
against the Ardientes

383
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,163
once we open the case.

384
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:37,958
We are fine-tuning Arthur's testimony.

385
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:41,128
And yes, we can use that evidence.

386
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:43,046
We can open the case soon.

387
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:47,050
[Camia] <i>Lily, I wish you were here.</i>

388
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:49,761
<i>We should've been celebrating with you.</i>

389
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:52,639
Mom, it's okay.

390
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:56,726
<i>The mere fact that you're all</i>
<i>happy makes me happy too.</i>

391
00:23:57,769 --> 00:23:58,728
[Ivy] <i>Diego.</i>

392
00:24:00,147 --> 00:24:01,523
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

393
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:04,985
I'm very impressed by what you did.

394
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:07,779
<i>Again, thank you.</i>

395
00:24:20,959 --> 00:24:24,379
<i>We almost lost everything.</i>

396
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:27,507
<i>Because of that bastard, Diego.</i>

397
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:30,510
<i>Your inheritance…</i>

398
00:24:32,179 --> 00:24:33,346
<i>the armory…</i>

399
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:35,307
<i>and everything in it.</i>

400
00:24:36,683 --> 00:24:38,852
<i>We almost lost it.</i>

401
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,231
Damn you, Diego.

402
00:24:45,066 --> 00:24:48,195
If you think you can stop me
from carrying out my plans

403
00:24:48,278 --> 00:24:49,905
because of that raid, you're wrong.

404
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,532
You got it all wrong.

405
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:55,660
You got it all wrong.

406
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:00,498
[woman] I miss Nimfa.

407
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:02,500
Life really is short.

408
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:05,837
So, if you want to do
something, just do it.

409
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:09,716
To be fair, Nimfa did that.

410
00:25:09,799 --> 00:25:12,219
Remember when we saw her with Diego?

411
00:25:12,302 --> 00:25:13,470
[woman] I remember!

412
00:25:14,137 --> 00:25:15,680
She said she loved Diego.

413
00:25:16,306 --> 00:25:18,725
Too bad, Diego didn't like her.

414
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:20,393
He even pushed her.

415
00:25:20,477 --> 00:25:22,520
That hurt Nimfa, you know.

416
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:25,482
No matter what she did,
Diego never seemed to like her.

417
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,566
I know.

418
00:25:28,735 --> 00:25:29,736
Ladies…

419
00:25:30,237 --> 00:25:31,404
-Was that true?
-Hi, Mayor.

420
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:33,281
-Hi, Mayor.
-Hello, Mayor.

421
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:36,034
Uh, it seems like you two know
something interesting.

422
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:38,620
Could you share it with me over dinner?

423
00:25:39,079 --> 00:25:41,998
[chuckles] Did you hear that?
Mayor invited us to dinner.

424
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:44,334
Sure, Mayor! What do you want to know?

425
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:47,003
Everything you know about Diego and Nimfa.

426
00:25:48,088 --> 00:25:48,922
Sure.

427
00:25:49,005 --> 00:25:50,257
-No problem.
-Let's go.

428
00:26:04,437 --> 00:26:07,107
Wait, why did you use
matte lipstick on her

429
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:08,650
and glossy lipstick on me?

430
00:26:08,733 --> 00:26:09,901
I want something like that.

431
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:13,280
Maybe they used glossy lipstick on you

432
00:26:13,363 --> 00:26:14,990
because you have dry lips, Emilia.

433
00:26:15,073 --> 00:26:17,659
But, if you want to use
my lipstick, no problem.

434
00:26:17,742 --> 00:26:19,452
-Go on, use it on her.
-Yes, ma'am.

435
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:21,496
Yeah, I like it! It looks nice.

436
00:26:23,164 --> 00:26:26,710
By the way, I noticed how nice
you've been to me lately.

437
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:29,671
Despite what I did

438
00:26:29,754 --> 00:26:32,465
sending a spy to infiltrate Diego's group.

439
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,217
Aren't you offended?

440
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:39,556
Well, as much as I'd want to be,

441
00:26:39,639 --> 00:26:41,558
it's not like your spy
accomplished anything.

442
00:26:41,641 --> 00:26:42,600
She died.

443
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:46,187
I know! She's dead.

444
00:26:46,813 --> 00:26:49,107
But, if Nimfa were alive,

445
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:51,526
I'm pretty sure she would've
found some dirt on you.

446
00:26:54,362 --> 00:26:55,405
[laughs]

447
00:26:56,656 --> 00:26:59,576
Emilia, we haven't even-- Go. Leave us.

448
00:26:59,659 --> 00:27:00,785
Quit eavesdropping.

449
00:27:02,620 --> 00:27:03,955
Emilia, we haven't even

450
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:07,667
recovered after what happened
at the Ardientes' armory.

451
00:27:08,168 --> 00:27:11,796
Shouldn't we be sticking together
during times like this?

452
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:15,300
Future mother-in-law,
I even lent you my lipstick!

453
00:27:17,844 --> 00:27:18,678
Okay.

454
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:21,139
Excuse me, Miss Aguas. You're up next.

455
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,849
-Okay.
-Go, you're needed inside.

456
00:27:22,932 --> 00:27:24,601
What do you think? Do I look okay?

457
00:27:25,685 --> 00:27:26,603
Yeah, you look fine.

458
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,688
[Ivy] Thanks! Excuse me.

459
00:27:31,941 --> 00:27:33,109
Aunt Claire, come!

460
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:36,738
You know I really smell something fishy.

461
00:27:38,948 --> 00:27:39,824
What do you mean?

462
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:43,036
I just know.

463
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:44,579
I can feel it, Auntie.

464
00:27:45,288 --> 00:27:47,582
If Nimfa hadn't died,

465
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:51,294
she would've found dirt on that woman.

466
00:27:51,669 --> 00:27:52,962
But, it doesn't matter.

467
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:57,467
I won't stop until I find
something about her.

468
00:27:57,842 --> 00:28:00,011
By hook, or by crook.

469
00:28:03,306 --> 00:28:05,600
A lot of people
are saying that this is going

470
00:28:05,683 --> 00:28:07,602
to be the political wedding of the decade.

471
00:28:07,685 --> 00:28:09,854
[giggles] Thank you.

472
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:12,690
But, you can't get away
without a little controversy.

473
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:15,527
Mayor Torillo,
the firearms in your possession

474
00:28:15,610 --> 00:28:16,861
were all confiscated.

475
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:19,364
That was just a misunderstanding.

476
00:28:19,989 --> 00:28:21,241
You know, whatever happens,

477
00:28:21,324 --> 00:28:24,786
that won't affect our wedding
or my candidacy.

478
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:27,539
[woman] But there's a pending case

479
00:28:27,622 --> 00:28:29,999
filed by your half-brother, Diego Torillo.

480
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:33,670
It won't affect our wedding
or my candidacy

481
00:28:35,088 --> 00:28:38,383
because whoever dares
to clash with Arnaldo

482
00:28:38,466 --> 00:28:39,467
-Ardiente Tor--
-Hon…

483
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:41,845
Hon.

484
00:28:41,928 --> 00:28:43,930
[tense music playing]

485
00:28:44,013 --> 00:28:45,014
Okay. Sorry.

486
00:28:47,350 --> 00:28:49,853
-Next question, please.
-Okay.

487
00:28:54,816 --> 00:28:55,817
[Ivy exhales]

488
00:28:57,777 --> 00:28:59,112
Camera's ready to roll?

489
00:28:59,529 --> 00:29:01,531
Let's begin, Mr. Torillo.

490
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:04,993
No matter how hard you try
to hide the truth,

491
00:29:05,660 --> 00:29:07,996
it will come out eventually.

492
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:10,331
I did not publicize the information

493
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:11,791
regarding the Ardientes' armory

494
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:13,334
just to ruin the mayor's reputation.

495
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:16,463
I did it because
it was the right thing to do.

496
00:29:18,006 --> 00:29:19,632
-It is illegal--
-[knocking on door]

497
00:29:20,425 --> 00:29:23,303
Mr. Torillo, we have a
warrant for your arrest

498
00:29:23,386 --> 00:29:25,138
for the murder of Nimfa Naig.

499
00:29:25,221 --> 00:29:25,972
[Loring] What?!

500
00:29:26,055 --> 00:29:27,599
[police officer] You have
the right to remain silent.

501
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:29,434
Everything you say or do
will be used against you.

502
00:29:29,517 --> 00:29:30,560
-What?
-You have the right…

503
00:29:30,643 --> 00:29:32,145
to an attorney.

504
00:29:32,228 --> 00:29:33,271
If you can't afford one,

505
00:29:33,354 --> 00:29:34,939
the government will provide one for you.

506
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:36,399
[Loring] What's this?

507
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:40,737
[tense music playing]

508
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:44,407
[camera shutter clicks]

509
00:29:47,076 --> 00:29:47,994
[Loring] Wait a minute.

510
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:51,289
Those allegations aren't true.

511
00:29:51,372 --> 00:29:53,291
You can't just arrest him.

512
00:29:53,374 --> 00:29:56,002
If you do, there will be trouble.

513
00:29:56,085 --> 00:29:58,046
I'm sure the Ardientes are behind this.

514
00:29:58,129 --> 00:29:59,756
They're afraid of losing the election,

515
00:29:59,839 --> 00:30:01,466
that's why they're framing Diego up.

516
00:30:01,549 --> 00:30:02,383
-She's right!
-Yeah!

517
00:30:02,467 --> 00:30:04,344
-[indistinct chatter]
-Calm down, everyone.

518
00:30:04,427 --> 00:30:06,346
We're just doing our job.

519
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:07,847
-Please come with us.
-No!

520
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:11,351
-Hold on just a second!
-Nanny, Uncle, everyone…

521
00:30:12,727 --> 00:30:13,770
I'm going with them.

522
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:15,980
But please don't worry,

523
00:30:16,064 --> 00:30:18,525
we all know I'm innocent.

524
00:30:19,651 --> 00:30:22,612
This is just a tactic used
by our enemies to bring us down.

525
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:25,657
We all know who really killed Nimfa.

526
00:30:26,115 --> 00:30:28,743
It was Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo,

527
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:30,829
and I will prove it.

528
00:30:32,539 --> 00:30:34,332
-Let's go, officer.
-Cuff him.

529
00:30:34,415 --> 00:30:36,334
You don't have to

530
00:30:36,417 --> 00:30:38,878
because the innocent
never run away from the law.

531
00:30:41,881 --> 00:30:43,216
Batch, don't worry.

532
00:30:43,299 --> 00:30:45,218
We'll manage your campaign
while you're away.

533
00:30:45,301 --> 00:30:47,136
-Thank you, Batch.
-Leave it to us.

534
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:49,514
-Nanny, Uncle…
-Take care of yourself.

535
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:50,932
Don't worry about me.

536
00:30:51,015 --> 00:30:51,850
-Diego…
-All right.

537
00:30:51,933 --> 00:30:52,725
-Let's get moving.
-Diego…

538
00:30:52,809 --> 00:30:54,018
I'll go with you to the precinct.

539
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:55,728
Who knows where they might take you.

540
00:30:55,812 --> 00:30:58,022
Sir, ma'am, I'll take care of him.

541
00:30:58,773 --> 00:30:59,983
-Don't worry.
-Ma'am…

542
00:31:00,066 --> 00:31:00,900
Everyone.

543
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:03,236
[Camia] Attorney, I need
to see you right away.

544
00:31:04,487 --> 00:31:05,321
[camera shutter clicks]

545
00:31:07,657 --> 00:31:09,325
-[Emilia] Papa!
-[Julio] Yes?

546
00:31:09,409 --> 00:31:13,204
This day deserves a celebration.

547
00:31:13,288 --> 00:31:14,122
[Arnaldo] Thank you.

548
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:15,748
-Emilia.
-Let's have champagne.

549
00:31:15,832 --> 00:31:16,624
[pops bottle]

550
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:18,793
This is not necessary.

551
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:21,170
Why not, Papa?

552
00:31:21,754 --> 00:31:23,256
You know, we should be celebrating now

553
00:31:23,339 --> 00:31:24,924
because our victory is certain.

554
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:28,136
After what Arnaldo did to
Diego… [sighs in relief]

555
00:31:28,845 --> 00:31:31,139
This election is just going to be easy.

556
00:31:31,222 --> 00:31:34,183
As easy as stealing candy from a baby.

557
00:31:35,768 --> 00:31:38,521
Hon, what did you do to him?

558
00:31:39,772 --> 00:31:42,150
Why are you so bothered, Ivy?

559
00:31:42,775 --> 00:31:44,527
Affected much?

560
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:45,403
[sighs]

561
00:31:45,486 --> 00:31:46,946
-[Raul] Arnaldo!
-[Emilia] You should be.

562
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:50,950
Arnaldo. What did you do to Diego?

563
00:31:54,704 --> 00:31:57,457
I had him arrested for Nimfa's murder.

564
00:31:59,792 --> 00:32:04,380
[tense music playing]

565
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:20,438
Mr. Diego Torillo, sign this.

566
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:23,358
I'll take your mug shot afterward.

567
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:29,739
I won't sign anything
until I talk to my lawyer.

568
00:32:30,281 --> 00:32:31,282
She'll be here soon.

569
00:32:31,532 --> 00:32:33,618
The judge already signed
your commitment order.

570
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:36,579
And the mobile patrol
is on its way to pick you up.

571
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:40,333
That's where they put murderers like you.

572
00:32:40,416 --> 00:32:42,085
Excuse me, but that's slander.

573
00:32:43,378 --> 00:32:44,295
I could press charges against you

574
00:32:44,379 --> 00:32:45,630
for what you said to my client.

575
00:32:46,005 --> 00:32:48,508
Atty. Georgina Fisher,
counsel of Mister Torillo.

576
00:32:48,841 --> 00:32:50,843
I'd like to speak
with my client privately.

577
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:53,596
And I don't need to explain to you

578
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:57,350
that you are obligated by the
law to grant us this request.

579
00:32:57,642 --> 00:33:00,436
Deny us of this right and you'll be sorry.

580
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:04,649
I will add you to the list
of dishonest cops

581
00:33:04,732 --> 00:33:06,234
who I've removed from their posts.

582
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:07,151
Excuse me.

583
00:33:12,615 --> 00:33:14,367
Emilia, all I'm saying is,

584
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:17,412
it's a good thing he was able to…

585
00:33:17,870 --> 00:33:19,539
seek justice for Nimfa's death.

586
00:33:20,623 --> 00:33:23,584
I just can't believe Diego
could do such a thing.

587
00:33:24,127 --> 00:33:25,962
Because it's true he wouldn't.

588
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:28,214
I know what you did, Arnaldo.

589
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:30,049
-You framed him up.
-You're right.

590
00:33:31,050 --> 00:33:32,093
It was a frame-up.

591
00:33:32,510 --> 00:33:34,303
And it was so easy.

592
00:33:35,888 --> 00:33:39,809
All because your favorite son's an idiot.

593
00:33:45,398 --> 00:33:47,025
[Arnaldo] <i>You know what to tell the cops?</i>

594
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:49,527
<i>Mayor…</i>

595
00:33:49,610 --> 00:33:52,030
<i>Don't worry. I've got your back.</i>

596
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:55,199
<i>Just don't make me mad.</i>

597
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:01,539
<i>The witnesses are ready.</i>

598
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:03,416
<i>Do you know where to bring</i>
<i>the girl's body?</i>

599
00:34:05,668 --> 00:34:07,211
<i>Okay. Get on it.</i>

600
00:34:21,809 --> 00:34:25,229
<i>Do you really think</i>
<i>this will work, Arnaldo?</i>

601
00:34:27,356 --> 00:34:28,983
<i>It will hold him off for a while.</i>

602
00:34:30,485 --> 00:34:32,070
<i>Long enough for me to win the election.</i>

603
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:34,655
<i>And who knows?</i>

604
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:38,117
<i>He might end up getting</i>
<i>into an accident in prison.</i>

605
00:34:38,659 --> 00:34:39,577
[chuckles]

606
00:34:40,411 --> 00:34:42,747
<i>That may be inevitable,</i>

607
00:34:42,830 --> 00:34:45,750
<i>but it's better for you to play it safe.</i>

608
00:34:46,667 --> 00:34:47,752
<i>I know.</i>

609
00:34:48,461 --> 00:34:49,879
<i>Like I said, don't worry, Grandpa.</i>

610
00:34:50,213 --> 00:34:51,464
<i>Everything's set.</i>

611
00:34:53,716 --> 00:34:54,842
<i>It's your show.</i>

612
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:59,263
[man] <i>Your plane tickets to</i>
<i>Singapore are in there.</i>

613
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:00,473
<i>Go on a vacation first.</i>

614
00:35:00,556 --> 00:35:02,308
<i>What will happen to Nimfa's case?</i>

615
00:35:02,391 --> 00:35:03,893
<i>My boss will make sure</i>

616
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,229
<i>the perpetrator will go to jail.</i>

617
00:35:06,312 --> 00:35:07,939
<i>Wait, who's your boss?</i>

618
00:35:08,022 --> 00:35:09,690
<i>It's not important who he is.</i>

619
00:35:10,358 --> 00:35:12,777
<i>But he will seek justice</i>
<i>for Nimfa's death.</i>

620
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:15,154
<i>Get inside the car.</i>

621
00:35:26,207 --> 00:35:27,959
<i>-Give me an update.</i>
<i>-It's all set, boss.</i>

622
00:35:34,549 --> 00:35:35,550
Hey.

623
00:35:36,050 --> 00:35:37,552
[scoffs] You look disappointed.

624
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:42,598
Turn that frown upside down.

625
00:35:43,266 --> 00:35:45,226
Or would you rather I killed him instead?

626
00:35:48,521 --> 00:35:51,732
[Emilia] Raul! Stop it! Raul!

627
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,234
-Hon!
-Go on!

628
00:35:53,317 --> 00:35:54,485
-That's enough!
-What?!

629
00:35:54,569 --> 00:35:56,654
-Raul!
-What?! Huh?! Come here.

630
00:35:56,737 --> 00:35:57,655
-Raul!
-Come here!

631
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:59,991
[Ivy] Hon! Emilia, stop Raul!

632
00:36:00,074 --> 00:36:01,367
-Raul!
-I'll kill him!

633
00:36:03,661 --> 00:36:04,829
-Stop right there!
-Hon!

634
00:36:05,329 --> 00:36:07,206
You bastard! What?!

635
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:09,083
[Emilia gasping]

636
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:11,669
[Emilia] Raul! Raul, wait!

637
00:36:11,752 --> 00:36:13,254
Don't go!

638
00:36:13,629 --> 00:36:15,214
You will pay for this!

639
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:16,299
Hon?

640
00:36:17,383 --> 00:36:19,969
You insolent piece of shit!

641
00:36:27,894 --> 00:36:29,103
-Are you okay?
-I'm okay.

642
00:36:29,187 --> 00:36:30,313
-I'm okay.
-Hon.

643
00:36:37,612 --> 00:36:39,030
[Georgina] An eyewitness

644
00:36:39,113 --> 00:36:41,407
and the body of the victim
at your headquarters?

645
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:44,493
They have a very compelling case
against you, Diego.

646
00:36:44,911 --> 00:36:47,079
Attorney, I'm being framed.

647
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:48,664
Arnaldo's behind all this.

648
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:52,251
He wants to taint my reputation,
so he can win the election.

649
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:54,086
But attorney, the truth is…

650
00:36:54,629 --> 00:36:56,923
Arnaldo killed Nimfa.

651
00:36:57,673 --> 00:36:59,091
Ivy told me herself.

652
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:01,177
Do you have this confession?

653
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:05,681
Well, it's hard to prove it
without evidence.

654
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:08,059
But, you're right.

655
00:37:08,142 --> 00:37:09,977
He does have motive to discredit you.

656
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:12,939
Because the Ardientes are scared of Diego.

657
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:16,442
They know that he can defeat Arnaldo.

658
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:19,528
Diego, you have the public's support.

659
00:37:19,612 --> 00:37:22,531
And we'll use the support of the people

660
00:37:22,615 --> 00:37:24,742
to spin this case against the Ardientes.

661
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:26,452
We'll hold a press conference.

662
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:29,914
So you can air your version of the story.

663
00:37:30,456 --> 00:37:32,041
We'll beat the Ardientes to it,

664
00:37:32,124 --> 00:37:34,293
so your name won't be ruined any further.

665
00:37:35,795 --> 00:37:38,923
But, I'm sorry, Diego. I can't
get you out of here for now.

666
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:41,676
I will try to delay your transfer
to the provincial jail,

667
00:37:41,759 --> 00:37:44,136
and I will do my best
to have your case dismissed.

668
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:46,514
Attorney, thank you very much.

669
00:37:48,391 --> 00:37:49,433
Thank you, attorney.

670
00:37:57,525 --> 00:37:59,151
DIEGO FOR THE NEW ARDIENTE

671
00:37:59,735 --> 00:38:00,820
[Pandoy sighs deeply]

672
00:38:00,903 --> 00:38:03,531
Those Ardientes are pure evil.

673
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:06,826
They'll do anything to get ahead.

674
00:38:06,909 --> 00:38:08,411
They'll try to manipulate

675
00:38:08,494 --> 00:38:11,289
anyone to believe that Diego is a killer.

676
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:14,000
What if Diego really killed my daughter?

677
00:38:14,375 --> 00:38:15,876
-What?
-Fernan.

678
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:17,586
Fernan.

679
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:21,549
You really believe Diego
is capable of killing someone?

680
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:25,011
[Pandoy] After everything
he's done for us?

681
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:27,305
He's just like Miss Aguas!

682
00:38:27,388 --> 00:38:29,974
She may have done a lot for the farmers,

683
00:38:30,808 --> 00:38:33,394
but who is she supporting?
Isn't she backing the Ardientes?

684
00:38:34,228 --> 00:38:36,188
There's a witness against Diego.

685
00:38:36,272 --> 00:38:39,567
No one will testify in court

686
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:41,235
if they aren't telling the truth.

687
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:43,362
You really think it's impossible, Fernan?

688
00:38:43,988 --> 00:38:47,658
The Ardientes can make
the impossible possible!

689
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:50,953
Possible or impossible,
I don't care about that!

690
00:38:51,037 --> 00:38:53,831
I just want someone to pay
for my daughter's death.

691
00:38:53,914 --> 00:38:55,041
They will!

692
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:57,043
And if it is Diego,

693
00:38:57,877 --> 00:39:00,504
prison won't be enough as punishment.

694
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:01,797
Fernan!

695
00:39:04,258 --> 00:39:05,259
Mister Fernan.

696
00:39:05,343 --> 00:39:07,762
[Pandoy sighs heavily]

697
00:39:08,387 --> 00:39:11,140
[indistinct chattering]

698
00:39:21,484 --> 00:39:23,277
My father was way out of line.

699
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:26,739
One more wrong move
and I'll finish him off.

700
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:30,451
Hon. Do you hear what you're saying?

701
00:39:31,077 --> 00:39:32,578
He's your dad.

702
00:39:32,661 --> 00:39:35,039
Well, he's useless to me.

703
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:36,874
And to this world.

704
00:39:36,957 --> 00:39:39,126
He's better off as fertilizer,

705
00:39:39,627 --> 00:39:41,670
just like Nimfa and, soon enough, Diego.

706
00:39:43,005 --> 00:39:44,006
Ouch!

707
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:45,591
What's wrong?

708
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:48,886
-Hey! What's your problem?
-You are!

709
00:39:49,678 --> 00:39:50,971
You're my problem.

710
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:55,810
See?

711
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:57,186
Look at yourself.

712
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:00,481
You can't help but show
your concern for Diego.

713
00:40:00,731 --> 00:40:01,857
You're thinking of him again.

714
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:03,901
I'm thinking of you!

715
00:40:04,193 --> 00:40:05,820
I'm concerned about you!

716
00:40:06,278 --> 00:40:08,155
You're getting out of control.

717
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:10,199
You're turning murder into a hobby!

718
00:40:12,743 --> 00:40:15,955
I'm just scared
because once we're married…

719
00:40:16,038 --> 00:40:20,918
What if I mess up the dish
I'm cooking or something?

720
00:40:21,001 --> 00:40:23,003
You might just shoot me!

721
00:40:25,506 --> 00:40:26,674
I could never hurt you.

722
00:40:27,758 --> 00:40:29,468
I told you I would never hurt you.

723
00:40:31,178 --> 00:40:33,431
[sighs] Hon, I'm so confused.

724
00:40:35,015 --> 00:40:36,892
I don't know because lately, I feel like…

725
00:40:37,768 --> 00:40:39,353
I don't know you anymore.

726
00:40:39,437 --> 00:40:41,814
It's like you have so many secrets.

727
00:40:41,897 --> 00:40:45,568
What if you killed somebody else
other than Nimfa?

728
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:49,655
So, tell me, hon.

729
00:40:51,574 --> 00:40:53,159
Aside from Nimfa…

730
00:40:55,453 --> 00:40:57,538
have you killed anyone else?

731
00:40:58,831 --> 00:41:00,458
Hon, tell me.

732
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:02,084
I don't want any secrets.

733
00:41:02,168 --> 00:41:04,920
[Carlotta screaming]

734
00:41:07,798 --> 00:41:09,675
Have you killed anyone else?

735
00:41:09,758 --> 00:41:13,762
[tense music playing]

736
00:41:16,557 --> 00:41:17,558
No.

737
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:22,146
I haven't killed anyone aside from Nimfa.

738
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:28,944
And I'm sorry for sounding
like a psychopath.

739
00:41:30,738 --> 00:41:32,323
I don't want you to be afraid of me.

740
00:41:33,407 --> 00:41:35,367
I want you to feel safe with me.

741
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:50,257
I sent Diego to jail
so I'd stop feeling jealous.

742
00:41:51,884 --> 00:41:53,511
I don't want to be angry with you anymore.

743
00:41:54,303 --> 00:41:55,554
So, I'll make sure…

744
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:58,891
that he never gets out of jail.

745
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:03,395
That way, he won't bother us again.

746
00:42:13,822 --> 00:42:15,616
I thought Raul had changed, Papa.

747
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:18,827
I thought he'd forgotten
about that bastard.

748
00:42:19,537 --> 00:42:21,038
I thought he was on our side!

749
00:42:21,789 --> 00:42:24,041
Blood is thicker than water, Emilia.

750
00:42:24,124 --> 00:42:26,418
But, Auntie, Arnaldo is also his son.

751
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:28,837
Why can't he love his two sons equally?

752
00:42:29,213 --> 00:42:31,840
Because he loved…

753
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:36,887
Diego's mother more than you!

754
00:42:37,846 --> 00:42:41,433
Just like all the other women
he has loved more than you.

755
00:42:41,767 --> 00:42:43,060
All the women in his life!

756
00:42:43,727 --> 00:42:44,853
You're so pathetic!

757
00:42:45,437 --> 00:42:47,273
For years, I have watched you!

758
00:42:47,898 --> 00:42:51,068
Begging, begging! Pleading for his love!

759
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:57,616
But that Raul has never
had any love to give you.

760
00:42:59,201 --> 00:43:01,787
What that man has given you…

761
00:43:02,705 --> 00:43:03,831
is pain.

762
00:43:04,331 --> 00:43:07,835
Pain for you, and for this family!

763
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,716
Congressman, your car is ready.

764
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:15,342
Good.

765
00:43:16,385 --> 00:43:17,469
Emilia.

766
00:43:19,096 --> 00:43:20,931
As lovesick as you are,

767
00:43:21,557 --> 00:43:23,601
you're still my daughter, and I love you.

768
00:43:24,143 --> 00:43:25,060
And tonight,

769
00:43:25,728 --> 00:43:27,313
I will end your misery.

770
00:43:28,272 --> 00:43:30,608
Papa, what do you mean?

771
00:43:31,817 --> 00:43:34,695
Just prepare a beautiful black dress.

772
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:39,950
And call your religious
female friends if you have any.

773
00:43:40,034 --> 00:43:40,909
No, Papa. You can't--

774
00:43:40,993 --> 00:43:44,788
[Julio] Because Raul's soul
will need a lot of people…

775
00:43:44,872 --> 00:43:47,458
-to pray for him.
-No, Papa! Please, don't!

776
00:43:48,125 --> 00:43:50,252
Please! Papa!

777
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:52,671
Papa!

778
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:54,131
Emilia, where are you going?

779
00:43:54,798 --> 00:43:57,009
I will save my husband, Auntie.

780
00:43:58,552 --> 00:43:59,762
Emilia!

781
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:05,517
[camera shutter clicks]

782
00:44:16,236 --> 00:44:17,237
Diego.

783
00:44:18,364 --> 00:44:21,283
Don't worry. We'll look into your case,

784
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:23,118
so you won't have to stay here for long.

785
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:24,328
That's right.

786
00:44:24,411 --> 00:44:26,580
Your transfer to the
provincial jail is postponed.

787
00:44:26,664 --> 00:44:27,915
You're safer here.

788
00:44:29,124 --> 00:44:32,544
Aunt Camia, please take care of
Nanny Loring and Uncle Pandoy.

789
00:44:33,379 --> 00:44:34,755
Tell them I'm fine.

790
00:44:36,382 --> 00:44:38,550
About Ivy… I know her.

791
00:44:39,093 --> 00:44:41,178
She'll find a way to get me out of here.

792
00:44:41,929 --> 00:44:44,598
Tell her not to do anything
that might put her in danger.

793
00:44:46,642 --> 00:44:48,018
Diego, keep your guard up here.

794
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:50,145
-Thank you, Aunt Camia.
-All right.

795
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:51,271
Attorney.

796
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:52,731
[Raul] Diego. Son.

797
00:44:53,607 --> 00:44:55,317
-Dad?
-How are you?

798
00:44:55,901 --> 00:44:56,819
I won't take long, sir.

799
00:44:57,986 --> 00:44:59,947
-How are you?
-What are you doing here, Dad?

800
00:45:01,740 --> 00:45:03,867
[Raul breathes heavily]

801
00:45:10,082 --> 00:45:13,043
Are you sure you don't want
to spend the night here with me?

802
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:18,424
My wounds will heal faster
if you stay here.

803
00:45:20,509 --> 00:45:22,678
Your wounds won't heal, hon.

804
00:45:23,470 --> 00:45:25,639
Because if I lay down beside you,

805
00:45:27,099 --> 00:45:28,100
I might get wild.

806
00:45:28,183 --> 00:45:29,601
Well, that's what I like.

807
00:45:30,018 --> 00:45:31,019
Wild.

808
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:33,814
[exhales sharply] Not now.

809
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:37,734
I know you're still furious
at your dad and Diego.

810
00:45:37,818 --> 00:45:41,280
You just might end up hurting me, instead.

811
00:45:44,283 --> 00:45:45,993
Okay, you're punishing me.

812
00:45:46,827 --> 00:45:47,870
I get it.

813
00:45:48,745 --> 00:45:50,831
-I'm punishing you?
-Mm-hm.

814
00:45:51,165 --> 00:45:52,124
No, hon.

815
00:45:53,167 --> 00:45:54,918
Because you wouldn't want…

816
00:45:55,669 --> 00:45:59,631
to be punished by Ivy Aguas.

817
00:46:05,971 --> 00:46:09,057
[tense music playing]

818
00:46:12,895 --> 00:46:14,062
-Ivy.
-[chuckles]

819
00:46:14,730 --> 00:46:16,482
-[Arnaldo chuckles]
-Sorry, hon.

820
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:19,401
I'm just like this when I'm in love.

821
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:23,322
Well, we only have to suffer a bit.

822
00:46:23,405 --> 00:46:24,615
It's almost the wedding.

823
00:46:25,449 --> 00:46:26,533
I can't wait.

824
00:46:27,117 --> 00:46:28,118
Me either.

825
00:46:29,161 --> 00:46:30,162
[moans]

826
00:46:31,163 --> 00:46:32,831
-Good night.
-Good night.

827
00:46:37,211 --> 00:46:39,087
[car engine turns over]

828
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:43,967
Raul. What are you doing here?

829
00:46:45,260 --> 00:46:46,887
I'm helping my son get out of here.

830
00:46:48,847 --> 00:46:50,933
Son, don't worry.

831
00:46:51,016 --> 00:46:52,309
I'll find a good lawyer

832
00:46:52,392 --> 00:46:54,978
to help you get out of here, okay?

833
00:46:55,479 --> 00:46:57,981
Thanks, Dad. But I've got a good lawyer.

834
00:46:58,065 --> 00:47:00,817
Raul. I'll take care of it.

835
00:47:01,735 --> 00:47:04,655
We can solve Diego's case faster

836
00:47:04,738 --> 00:47:06,031
if you won't get involved.

837
00:47:06,698 --> 00:47:09,284
Just go back to hiding
behind the Ardientes.

838
00:47:09,368 --> 00:47:11,703
But here's the thing, Camia. He's my son.

839
00:47:11,787 --> 00:47:14,122
So I have the right
to help him get out of here.

840
00:47:14,206 --> 00:47:15,666
Yes, you're his father.

841
00:47:15,749 --> 00:47:17,668
A father who doesn't know how to be one.

842
00:47:17,751 --> 00:47:20,504
A father who blindly
follows the Ardientes.

843
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:22,339
[scoffs] I don't know what your

844
00:47:22,422 --> 00:47:23,674
-problem is.
-Dad. Dad.

845
00:47:25,509 --> 00:47:27,761
Please. You should leave.

846
00:47:30,764 --> 00:47:33,225
-I'll prove it to you.
-You won't prove anything to me

847
00:47:33,308 --> 00:47:35,811
or anyone as long as you're
under the Ardientes' thumb.

848
00:47:36,603 --> 00:47:37,980
-Of course, he wouldn't…
-Emilia.

849
00:47:38,063 --> 00:47:39,439
leave our side.

850
00:47:39,898 --> 00:47:41,483
-You know why, Camia?
-Emilia.

851
00:47:41,858 --> 00:47:43,610
Because he's all mine.

852
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,120
Grandpa?

853
00:48:02,713 --> 00:48:03,755
[phone ringing]

854
00:48:05,215 --> 00:48:06,300
[phone ringing]

855
00:48:07,759 --> 00:48:08,844
[phone ringing]

856
00:48:11,680 --> 00:48:13,640
-Arnaldo.
-Grandpa, where are you?

857
00:48:14,308 --> 00:48:18,437
Oh, I'm at Raul's final resting place.

858
00:48:19,605 --> 00:48:20,647
Wait for me. I'll be there.

859
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:22,232
I want to get back at that bastard.

860
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:23,692
[sighs] No, no, no.

861
00:48:23,775 --> 00:48:26,737
You sit this one out, Arnaldo.

862
00:48:27,487 --> 00:48:29,239
<i>I don't think you should see this.</i>

863
00:48:29,323 --> 00:48:33,327
You might end up
feeling sorry for your father

864
00:48:33,410 --> 00:48:34,661
after what I'll do to him,

865
00:48:34,745 --> 00:48:36,538
<i>or even stop me.</i>

866
00:48:36,622 --> 00:48:37,706
<i>Besides,</i>

867
00:48:37,789 --> 00:48:40,500
you've got too much blood
on your hands already.

868
00:48:41,251 --> 00:48:44,588
I think it's about time I took over
the dirty jobs once again

869
00:48:44,671 --> 00:48:45,672
just like this one.

870
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:47,841
Well, make sure you punish him good.

871
00:48:47,924 --> 00:48:49,968
Oh, don't worry. I will.

872
00:48:50,552 --> 00:48:51,678
<i>In the meantime,</i>

873
00:48:51,762 --> 00:48:55,015
keep an eye on Miss Aguas, okay?

874
00:48:56,266 --> 00:48:57,434
[exhales sharply]

875
00:48:57,517 --> 00:48:58,477
Okay.

876
00:49:05,525 --> 00:49:06,652
Mm?

877
00:49:06,735 --> 00:49:09,946
Congressman. We found where
Ma'am Emilia and Raul are.

878
00:49:11,031 --> 00:49:12,032
Good.

879
00:49:12,532 --> 00:49:14,159
Bring both of them here.

880
00:49:14,868 --> 00:49:16,620
-Now.
-Yes, sir.

881
00:49:16,703 --> 00:49:20,457
[dramatic music playing]

882
00:49:26,171 --> 00:49:28,465
<i>They framed me</i>
<i>for the murder of Nimfa Naig.</i>

883
00:49:28,548 --> 00:49:30,050
<i>Why would they do that to you?</i>

884
00:49:30,133 --> 00:49:32,094
<i>To ensure that their side will win.</i>

885
00:49:32,177 --> 00:49:34,137
<i>Let's do a pre-election survey.</i>

886
00:49:34,221 --> 00:49:36,682
<i>Whoever wins there is the one</i>
<i>who's telling the truth.</i>

887
00:49:36,765 --> 00:49:38,016
<i>Now, who are they going to choose?</i>

888
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:41,186
<i>A criminal or an honest</i>
<i>politician like me?</i>

889
00:49:41,269 --> 00:49:44,690
[Julio] <i>How did this dog beat you?</i>

890
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:46,400
[Camia] <i>He needs to get out of that prison</i>

891
00:49:46,483 --> 00:49:49,444
<i>because I know the Ardientes</i>
<i>are plotting to get rid of him.</i>

892
00:49:49,528 --> 00:49:52,280
[Ivy] <i>I have the evidence</i>
<i>that will set him free.</i>

893
00:49:52,364 --> 00:49:55,200
[Arnaldo on voice memo]
<i>No. I haven't killed anyone</i>

894
00:49:55,283 --> 00:49:56,451
<i>aside from Nimfa.</i>

895
00:49:56,535 --> 00:49:58,870
<i>I will tell the world that I am Lily.</i>

896
00:49:58,954 --> 00:50:02,082
[theme music playing]
